diff --git a/memory/note/n_1027_c35c.md b/memory/note/n_1027_c35c.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..2d69d39e1d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/memory/note/n_1027_c35c.md
@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+---
+id: "n_1027_c35c"
+type: "note"
+title: "Shell-job near-miss test fixtures: NEVER build a stale id by blind-suffixing a minted id (e.g. `entry.id.substring(0, len-2) + 'zz'`) — `newShellJobId`'s random base36 tail ends in 'zz' once every ~1296 starts, the \"stale\" id then IS the exact id, and lookup rightly answers `ShellJobHit` instead of `ShellJobNearMiss` (loud red in `shell_jobs_test.dart` AC1 and 2 of 3 `bash_job_resolution_test.dart` AC1 fixtures, silent coverage loss elsewhere). Incident class hit twice: red main run 38120494810 (AC5 stop test) and tag-train v1.0.708 run 43006085893 → gh-2113 (hostile-env leg, 1 failure in 13,775; also failed the `Quality gate` aggregate and cascaded `Advance vpinned marker`). Fix (test-only, commit f2f8d58 on ai/gh-2113): force the retained id with `env.forcedIds = ['sh-1-aaaa']` before `registry.start` in ALL near-miss fixtures — the idiom is commented in-place at all four sites; extend the same treatment to any new near-miss fixture."
+author: "agent"
+date: "2026-11-11T11:22:20.115742Z"
+area: "project"
+topics: []
+source: "agent"
+accessCount: 0
+importance: 0.5
+tags: ["#note", "#source_agent", "ci", "testing", "flake", "shell-jobs", "gh-2113", "gotcha"]
+---
+
+
+# Note: n_1027_c35c
+
+Shell-job near-miss test fixtures: NEVER build a stale id by blind-suffixing a minted id (e.g. `entry.id.substring(0, len-2) + 'zz'`) — `newShellJobId`'s random base36 tail ends in 'zz' once every ~1296 starts, the "stale" id then IS the exact id, and lookup rightly answers `ShellJobHit` instead of `ShellJobNearMiss` (loud red in `shell_jobs_test.dart` AC1 and 2 of 3 `bash_job_resolution_test.dart` AC1 fixtures, silent coverage loss elsewhere). Incident class hit twice: red main run 38120494810 (AC5 stop test) and tag-train v1.0.708 run 43006085893 → gh-2113 (hostile-env leg, 1 failure in 13,775; also failed the `Quality gate` aggregate and cascaded `Advance vpinned marker`). Fix (test-only, commit f2f8d58 on ai/gh-2113): force the retained id with `env.forcedIds = ['sh-1-aaaa']` before `registry.start` in ALL near-miss fixtures — the idiom is commented in-place at all four sites; extend the same treatment to any new near-miss fixture.
+
+**By:** [[agent]]
+**Date:** 2026-11-11T11:22:20.115742Z
+**Area:** [[project|project]]
